 "notes": [
  "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
  "In the image the joystick's five header pins sit in one breadboard column, which would short them in the catalogue model. I put them in row j of five adjacent columns (6 to 10, bank b) instead. Each jumper wire goes in row i of the same column as its joystick pin.",
  "Wiring follows the circuit image: red 5V to VCC, yellow A0 to VERT, green A1 to HORZ, blue pin 6 to SEL, black GND to GND. The text says the x-axis is on A0, but the image puts A0 on VERT, and I followed the image.",
  "The optional status LED circuit is not in the image. I wired it as pin 5, then wire6, then the 220 ohm resistor, then the LED anode. The LED cathode goes by wire7 to GND.2 on the Leonardo. The column numbers used on the breadboard (20 to 22, bank t) are my own choice.",
  "The joystick's SEL line is its built-in pushbutton, wired to pin 6 with no external pulldown. The tutorial says a pulldown may not be needed for a joystick like this, so none is included.",
  "The optional second pushbutton and its 10k pulldown on D3 are not built."
 ],
